Jordan,

I've been looking at the admission webhook logs and there's something odd.
The webhook was redeployed at 02:50 UTC with the new validateNamespace()
handler, and there's a gap in the audit log between 03:08 and 03:14 where
several requests appear to have been processed with stale cache entries.

I'm not 100% sure yet but it looks like a race condition in the cache
invalidation path. When multiple requests arrive simultaneously for pods
in the payments namespace, the goroutines may be reading from a stale
namespace object before the mutation is committed. This would explain the
intermittent admission failures we're seeing.

Combined with the helm chart memory regression, any pod that gets
admitted incorrectly and then has only 512Mi available will OOM immediately
under the payment-svc startup load.

I've asked the vendor about the chart version. Will update when I hear back.

